This test checks that header unparsing remains stable when the frontend
normalizes a missing `template<>` header for an out-of-class member
specialization while the associated header also uses `std::vector<bool>`.

The regression guards two interactions:
1. `-rose:unparseHeaderFiles` must still emit the application header.
2. The normalized specialization must round-trip through the backend with
   the required `template<>` header present in the unparsed source.
